# qr-dining nightly backup — cron alternative to the systemd timer.
# Install with:  sudo crontab -e   (or drop in /etc/cron.d/qr-dining-backup)
#
# Loads DATABASE_URL + provider creds from /etc/qr-dining/backup.env, runs at 02:30,
# and appends output to a log.
#
# ALERTING, precisely: BackupFailed watches the Prometheus textfile metric
# qr_dining_backup_last_run_status, which nightly-backup.sh writes itself via its
# ERR trap. NOTHING watches the marker file below — it is a breadcrumb for a human
# reading the host, not a monitored signal. (An earlier version of this comment
# claimed otherwise.)
#
# Blind spot worth knowing: if the env file is missing or unreadable, the script
# exits at its DATABASE_URL guard BEFORE the ERR trap is installed, so the status
# metric keeps reporting the last good run and BackupFailed never fires. Only
# BackupTooOld catches that, 36h later. Same if cron never fires at all. See
# docs/OPERATIONS.md §5 and docs/history/restore-verification-report-2026-09-12.md
# (finding R-3).

30 2 * * * root set -a; . /etc/qr-dining/backup.env; set +a; /opt/qr-dining/backend/scripts/nightly-backup.sh >> /var/log/qr-dining-backup.log 2>&1 || touch /var/run/qr-dining-backup.failed
